 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two, three and four",
     "texto": [
      "In sentences in the nominative, **один/одна/одно** agrees in gender and the noun is in the singular: **один стол**, **одна книга**, **одно окно**. With **2–4**, the noun is in the genitive singular: **два брата**, **две сестры**, **три города**. With **5–20**, it is in the genitive plural: **пять книг**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Compound numbers",
     "texto": [
      "In the nominative, look at the last two digits: if they end in **1** (except **11**), the noun is in the nominative singular; if they end in **2–4** (except **12–14**), in the genitive singular; in the other cases, in the genitive plural. Examples: **21 год**, **22 года**, **25 лет**, **111 лет**, **121 год**, **122 года**.",
      "The numeral **один** agrees with gender: **21 год**, **21 книга**, **21 окно**. These patterns are for the nominative; in other cases the forms of the numeral and of the noun change."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking about quantities",
     "texto": [
      "**Сколько** («how many») and **мало** («few») take the genitive plural with countable nouns: **Сколько у тебя братьев?**; **У меня мало друзей**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
